claim=dict(id=claimid,kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='Within one fixed EPaxos configuration and crash-fault history, once a command batch is committed for a replica-row/instance, any later commitment for that same row/instance at a nonfailed participant must contain the same ordered command batch, including across per-instance recovery and higher ballot promises.',source_ids=['S-formation','S-commit','S-recovery','S-readme','S-run'],scope=dict(description='Per-instance command decision agreement across recovery in a five-node volatile configuration tolerating up to two crash failures.',assumptions=['Static N=5,F=2 and distinct participant identities','At most one crash in the selected history; no Byzantine inputs or restart','Messages are actual emitted bytes and dispatched in a schedule allowed by per-type protocol channels'],excluded=['Linearizability or client-visible outcomes','Persistent crash restart','Automatic termination or a numeric recovery deadline']),pending=[],grounding=g('S-formation marks an instance COMMITTED only after its support condition and propagates the command batch. S-commit refuses to replace established committed/executed instances. S-recovery explicitly selects committed support as its first preservation case rather than treating a new promise as a new object identity. S-readme identifies this implementation as corrected EPaxos within a replicated-state-machine repository, and S-run derives crash-fault capacity. The required agreement concerns the existing row/instance identity across these mechanisms; a higher ballot is authority context, not a fresh command slot. The check compares complete ordered command content rather than equating ballot numbers or status labels.','Same configuration and instance, both observed decisions at nodes that have not failed.'))
